.TH LIBDAQ_ALERT 3 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-bigredbox 2.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
libdaq_alert, daq_alert_send, daq_alert_strerror \- C library for sending Big Red Box alerts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <daq_alert.h>
.PP
.B #define DAQ_ALERT_PORT 37020
.B #define DAQ_ALERT_BROADCAST_IP \(dq255.255.255.255\(dq
.PP
.B typedef enum {
.B "    DAQ_ALERT_OK         =  0,"
.B "    DAQ_ALERT_ERR_SOCKET = \-1,"
.B "    DAQ_ALERT_ERR_SEND   = \-2,"
.B "    DAQ_ALERT_ERR_FORMAT = \-3"
.B } DaqAlertResult;
.PP
.BI "DaqAlertResult daq_alert_send(const char *" system_id ,
.BI "                              const char *" message ,
.BI "                              const char *" broadcast_ip ,
.BI "                              uint16_t " port );
.PP
.BI "const char *daq_alert_strerror(DaqAlertResult " result );
.fi
.PP
Link with
.B \-ldaq_alert
(static archive
.IR libdaq_alert.a ,
CMake target
.BR daq_alert_c );
on Windows also
.BR ws2_32 .
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B daq_alert_send()
builds the alert datagram
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
{"system_id":"\fIsystem_id\fR","timestamp":"\fIYYYY\-MM\-DDTHH:MM:SS\fR","message":"\fImessage\fR"}
.fi
.RE
.PP
and sends it as one UDP datagram to
.IR broadcast_ip : port
with
.B SO_BROADCAST
set, on a socket created and closed within the call.
A NULL or empty
.I broadcast_ip
means
.BR DAQ_ALERT_BROADCAST_IP ;
a
.I port
of 0 means
.BR DAQ_ALERT_PORT .
The timestamp is the sender's local time with no zone offset, to the second.
.PP
.I system_id
and
.I message
are escaped for JSON:
.BR \e" ,
.BR \e\e ,
.BR \en ,
.BR \er ,
.B \et
as short escapes, every other byte below 0x20 (including backspace and form
feed) as
.BR \eu00XX ,
and all other bytes, including DEL and UTF\-8 sequences, copied unchanged.
Invalid UTF\-8 is passed through, and the listener then discards the datagram
as undecodable.
.PP
.B daq_alert_strerror()
returns a static string describing
.IR result .
.PP
The C++ binding
.BR libdaq_alert_cpp (3)
and the Python binding
.BR daq_alert (3)
produce datagrams that decode to the same JSON object; the bytes differ (see
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-api (7)).
.SH RETURN VALUE
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_OK
The datagram was handed to the kernel.
UDP gives no delivery guarantee.
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_ERR_SOCKET
.BR socket (2)
failed.
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_ERR_SEND
.BR sendto (2)
failed.
.TP
.B DAQ_ALERT_ERR_FORMAT
A field exceeded the escape buffer, or the whole payload exceeded 4095 bytes.
Nothing is sent.
.SH NOTES
.TP
.B Address parsing
.I broadcast_ip
is converted with
.BR inet_addr (3).
A string it cannot parse, including any host name, yields
.BR INADDR_NONE ,
which is 255.255.255.255: the alert is sent as a local limited broadcast and
the call returns
.BR DAQ_ALERT_OK .
Pass a dotted\-quad address only, and check it yourself.
.TP
.B Size limits
Each of
.I system_id
and
.I message
may be at most 2041 bytes after escaping; the Python binding has no such
limit.
Keep messages short: the text is shown in a window and read aloud in full.
.TP
.B NULL arguments
.I system_id
and
.I message
must not be NULL; they are dereferenced without a check.
.TP
.B Threads
The function keeps no state and may be called from several threads.
.TP
.B Reach
The default destination is the limited broadcast address, which never
crosses a router.
To reach a listener on another subnet, send to that host's unicast address.
.PP
Version 1.0.0 of the sender libraries
.RI ( libs/CMakeLists.txt ),
shipped with mu2edaq\-bigredbox 2.0.0.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <daq_alert.h>

int report(const char *what)
{
    DaqAlertResult rc = daq_alert_send("DAQ\-NODE\-01", what, NULL, 0);
    if (rc != DAQ_ALERT_OK)
        fprintf(stderr, "alert failed: %s\en", daq_alert_strerror(rc));
    return rc;
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Build and install from the repository:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
cmake \-S libs \-B libs/build && cmake \-\-build libs/build \-j
cmake \-\-install libs/build \-\-prefix /opt/mu2edaq
cc \-I/opt/mu2edaq/include app.c /opt/mu2edaq/lib/libdaq_alert.a
.fi
.RE
